<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Intentionally empty. dotfix runs `brew`, `git` and `security` as child
  processes (Command::new), which needs no entitlement at all — the
  hardened-runtime entitlements that exist (allow-unsigned-executable-memory,
  disable-library-validation) govern code loaded into THIS process's own
  address space (dylibs, JIT'd memory), not what a spawned child process can
  do, so they would grant nothing this app needs while permanently widening
  its own attack surface (disable-library-validation in particular would let
  the signed, notarized binary load dylibs signed by anyone, not just the
  same Team ID).

  This file (and the hardened runtime it enables) stays required for
  notarization. Add an entitlement here only if notarization fails with an
  error that names it specifically, and record which error prompted it:
    - none recorded yet.
-->
<dict/>
</plist>
